{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.CentralExtensionObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CentralExtensionObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.GroupExtension.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Group"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.obstruction_section_change","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.obstruction_section_change","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CentralExtensionObstruction.lean#L196-L225","doc":"**Section independence (the obstruction is a class).** Replacing the\nsection `σ` by any other section `σ'` multiplies the obstruction by the\n2-coboundary of some `t : H → A`, so the class of `c` in `H²(H, A)` (trivial\naction) does not depend on the choice of section. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.exists_lift_iff_coboundary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.exists_lift_iff_coboundary","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CentralExtensionObstruction.lean#L143-L194","doc":"**Lifting criterion.** `φ` lifts through `E → G` iff its obstruction is a\n2-coboundary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.obstruction_cocycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.obstruction_cocycle","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CentralExtensionObstruction.lean#L115-L141","doc":"**The obstruction is a 2-cocycle** (trivial action; `A` is central). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.obstruction_spec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.obstruction_spec","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CentralExtensionObstruction.lean#L102-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.obstruction","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CentralExtensionObstruction.lean#L97-L100","doc":"The obstruction cochain `c g h ∈ A`, the unique element with\n`σ (φ g) * σ (φ h) = inl (c g h) * σ (φ (g * h))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.rightHom_defect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.rightHom_defect","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CentralExtensionObstruction.lean#L91-L95","doc":"The element `σ(φ g) σ(φ h) σ(φ(gh))⁻¹` lies over `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.rightHom_inl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.rightHom_inl","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CentralExtensionObstruction.lean#L82-L86","doc":"`inl` maps into the kernel of `rightHom`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.exists_inl_of_rightHom_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.exists_inl_of_rightHom_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CentralExtensionObstruction.lean#L75-L80","doc":"An element of `E` lying over `1 ∈ G` is in the image of `inl`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}